---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import TopicCluster from '../components/TopicCluster.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import PathwayCard from '../components/PathwayCard.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import EditorialPhoto from '../components/EditorialPhoto.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import seekingImage from '../assets/images/lala/lala-golden-hour-seeking.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="She Who Remembers | The Book"
  description="She Who Remembers is a book of personal wisdom on sovereignty, embodiment, self-trust, boundaries, and feminine wisdom that does not abandon discernment."
>
  <Hero
    heading="She Who Remembers"
    lede="Lessons in Power, Presence, and Remembering Who You Are"
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      A work of nonfiction and personal wisdom: language for the woman who is done living as a
      well-managed edition of herself, and is not interested in replacing one performance with
      another.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="dark" atmosphere={true} spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <p class="source-line">
        The book can stand alone. It is also the well the rest of this work drinks from.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What the book is">
        <p>Not a manifesto to join. A companion for remembering.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <em>She Who Remembers</em> explores sovereignty, shadow, embodiment, intuition,
          boundaries, voice, sisterhood, lineage, transmission, and legacy. It is written for
          reading, not for collecting a personality.
        </p>
        <p>
          Publication details, retailers, and price are not listed here yet. When a way to
          obtain the book is ready, it will be named plainly. Until then, the ideas are already
          at work in the path, the courses, and private guidance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-breath">
        <EditorialPhoto
          src={seekingImage}
          variant="seeking"
          alt="Lala seated in evening light in a cream wrap, looking toward the sky."
        />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Who it is for">
        <p>Recognition, not crisis, is enough.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ul class="fit">
        <li>An old identity still functions, and no longer fits.</li>
        <li>Self-trust has gone quiet under competence, caretaking, or too much advice.</li>
        <li>Performing strength has become exhausting, and you want a different kind of power.</li>
        <li>You want spiritual depth without abandoning discernment, evidence, or your own mind.</li>
        <li>A new chapter is already underway, named or not.</li>
        <li>You want language for what you already sense, not a personality transplant.</li>
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="The five parts">
        <p>
          A spine for the book, not a demand that your life match the sequence. Fuller
          philosophy of the path lives on{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/the-work')}>The Work</TextLink>. These notes are for the
          book itself.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ol class="parts">
        <li>
          <p class="parts__roman">Part I</p>
          <h3>The Awakening</h3>
          <p class="parts__sub">Reclaiming Inner Sovereignty</p>
          <p>
            The return of an inner vote: noticing where identity has been organized around
            usefulness, and where a quieter authorship is trying to speak.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="parts__roman">Part II</p>
          <h3>The Descent</h3>
          <p class="parts__sub">Meeting the Shadow</p>
          <p>
            What was sent underground to remain acceptable. Anger, jealousy, fear, and hidden
            truths are met so they no longer have to run the schedule from below.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="parts__roman">Part III</p>
          <h3>The Embodiment</h3>
          <p class="parts__sub">Walking as the Divine</p>
          <p>
            Insight leaving the page and entering breath, speech, and choice. Divinity here is
            not costume. It is presence that can inhabit an ordinary life.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="parts__roman">Part IV</p>
          <h3>The Ascent</h3>
          <p class="parts__sub">Integration & Multiplication</p>
          <p>
            Life returning to the center. What has been integrated does not stay private as a
            secret. It begins to move through how you create, relate, and take up space.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="parts__roman">Part V</p>
          <h3>The Legacy</h3>
          <p class="parts__sub">The Future Is Hers</p>
          <p>
            Continuation: what is handed on, interrupted, or made because a woman became
            conscious. The future named here is authorship, not a guaranteed plot.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container>
      <SectionIntro heading="Selected themes">
        <p>Threads that run through the book, without requiring you to collect them all.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="topics">
        <TopicCluster title="Sovereignty">Self-trust, power, and identity that no longer outsources the last decision.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Shadow">Anger, jealousy, fear, and the truths that were hidden to keep the peace.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Boundaries">The Sacred No, and the energetic sovereignty of a cleaner yes.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Embodiment">Body, breath, sensuality, and presence that can stay in the room.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Intuition">The Oracle and the Architect: listening, then evaluating, without a civil war.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Sisterhood">Connection without idealizing women, or disappearing to keep them close.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Voice">Expression, truth, and speech that does not rush to make itself palatable.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Legacy">Transmission, lineage, and contribution that does not require a stage.</TopicCluster>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container>
      <SectionIntro heading="Oracle and Architect">
        <p>The work does not ask you to choose intuition over logic, or logic over knowing.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="split">
        <Card variant="blush">
          <h3>The Oracle</h3>
          <p>
            Listens. Receives the inner signal, the body cue, the image, the unease that arrives
            before a tidy argument. It is not treated as infallible. It is treated as data that
            deserves a hearing.
          </p>
        </Card>
        <Card>
          <h3>The Architect</h3>
          <p>
            Evaluates. Tests timing, consequence, evidence, and the life that has to carry the
            choice. Strategy without listening becomes a cage. Listening without evaluation
            becomes a mood.
          </p>
        </Card>
      </div>
      <div class="council">
        <p>
          Together they support discernment. In practice this can look like a Double Council: a
          pause in which both voices are consulted before the mouth agrees. Not a ritual you
          must adopt. A way of refusing to exile either half of your intelligence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container>
      <SectionIntro heading="From book to experience">
        <p>
          Reading can be enough. For those who want the ideas in a lived container, these are
          doors, not upgrades you are failing if you skip.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="offer-grid">
        <PathwayCard
          kicker="Voice"
          heading="The Sacred No"
          ctaLabel="Explore The Sacred No"
          ctaHref={withBase('/courses/the-sacred-no')}
        >
          <p>Boundaries, communication, and a cleaner relationship to yes and no.</p>
        </PathwayCard>
        <PathwayCard
          kicker="Self"
          heading="The Remembering"
          ctaLabel="Explore The Remembering"
          ctaHref={withBase('/courses/the-remembering')}
        >
          <p>The deeper journey of identity, embodiment, and self-trust.</p>
        </PathwayCard>
        <PathwayCard
          kicker="Purpose"
          heading="Legacy in Motion"
          ctaLabel="Explore Legacy in Motion"
          ctaHref={withBase('/courses/legacy-in-motion')}
        >
          <p>Contribution, lived wisdom, and what continues because you became conscious.</p>
        </PathwayCard>
        <PathwayCard
          kicker="Room"
          heading="Private Guidance"
          ctaLabel="Explore Private Guidance"
          ctaHref={withBase('/private-guidance')}
        >
          <p>Individualized support when the threshold needs more space than a group path.</p>
        </PathwayCard>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="A note on scope">
        <p>Wisdom is not a license to replace care.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The book offers personal wisdom and educational material. It is not a substitute for
          psychological care, medical advice, or legal advice. If those are needed, they remain
          needed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If the book is the well, the path is how some women drink"
    primary={{ label: 'Explore the Work', href: withBase('/the-work') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Begin Here', href: withBase('/begin-here') }}
  >
    <p>
      There is no purchase link on this page yet. The work is still available to walk, whether
      or not the book is in your hands.
    </p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .source-line {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-quote);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: var(--leading-heading);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .prose,
  .council {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .photo-breath {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .council {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .fit {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .fit li {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .fit li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .fit li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.7em;
    width: 0.4rem;
    height: 0.4rem;
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .parts {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .parts li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: var(--border-width) solid var(--gold-border);
  }

  .parts__roman {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xs);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--text-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-accent);
  }

  .parts h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .parts__sub {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--text-ui);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-ui);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .topics,
  .offer-grid,
  .split {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .split h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .topics,
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }

    .offer-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
